    "text": "To determine how many full glasses of juice Daniel can serve, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total amount of juice Daniel has.\n2. Determine how many full glasses can be served with the total amount of juice.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total amount of juice. Daniel has 5 jars of juice, and each jar contains 2 liters. Since there are 1000 milliliters in a liter, we can convert the total amount of juice to milliliters:\n\\[ 5 \\text{ jars} \\times 2 \\text{ liters/jar} \\times 1000 \\text{ milliliters/liter} = 10000 \\text{ milliliters} \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine how many full glasses can be served with 10000 milliliters of juice. Each glass can hold up to 250 milliliters, so we divide the total amount of juice by the capacity of one glass:\n\\[ 10000 \\text{ milliliters} \\div 250 \\text{ milliliters/glass} = 40 \\text{ glasses} \\]\n\nTherefore, Daniel can serve \\(\\boxed{40}\\) full glasses of juice.",
